From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:47:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] dt-bindings: soundwire: qcom: document
 qcom,ports-ch-mask

The driver has parsed qcom,ports-ch-mask since commit 386668abb9c4
("soundwire: qcom: add DT-driven per-port ch_mask
(qcom,ports-ch-mask)") but the property was never added to the
schema.  Board DTs that use it currently fail dtbs_check with
"Unevaluated properties are not allowed".  Document it as an
optional uint8 array bounded by the same [3..17] port count that
the other per-port arrays use.

Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit d8ef4de40dce78c344f5bf28cd3f5a1ed8a124cf)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/soundwire/qcom,soundwire.yaml | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soundwire/qcom,soundwire.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soundwire/qcom,soundwire.yaml
index 9250999515b4..2ddd58d85937 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soundwire/qcom,soundwire.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soundwire/qcom,soundwire.yaml
@@ -253,6 +253,17 @@ properties:
     minimum: 1
     maximum: 8
 
+  qcom,ports-ch-mask:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
+    description:
+      Per-port intrinsic SoundWire channel mask.  Used when programming
+      the master DPn PORT_CTRL channel-enable field so a port's slot
+      layout (e.g. stereo PDM) is transmitted independently of the PCM
+      stream's channel count.  0xff means the option is not applicable
+      for that port.
+    minItems: 3
+    maxItems: 17
+
   label:
     maxItems: 1
 
